1	<!-- kinematic-diagram-generator/SKILL.md -->
2	---
3	name: kinematic-diagram-generator
4	description: Generate professional two-panel SVG kinematic diagrams and Grubler DOF analysis in dark-mode HTML for planar or spatial mechanisms. Use when the user requests HTML visualizations of mechanical linkages, parallel robots, closed loops, or degree-of-freedom breakdowns showing separate link and joint schematics.
5	---
6	
7	# Kinematic Diagram Generator
8	
9	A specialized compiler and workflow for analyzing kinematic mechanisms (links, joints, mobility) and rendering self-contained, high-contrast dark-mode HTML blueprints without conversational preamble or external raster images.
10	
11	## When to Use
12	
13	- User provides an image or description of a mechanical linkage, parallel robot, closed-loop mechanism, or planar/spatial kinematic chain.
14	- User asks to draw, visualize, calculate, or generate kinematic diagrams or degree-of-freedom (DOF) analysis in HTML/SVG format.
15	- User sends a markdown template or asks for a dual-panel breakdown of Links vs Joints.
16	
17	## Strict Output Constraints
18	
19	- ZERO conversational preamble or trailing explanation: output MUST begin immediately with `<!-- [mechanism_name].html -->` followed by `<!DOCTYPE html>` inside a copiable `html` code block, ending with `</html>`.
20	- STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Calling image generation tools (e.g. DALL-E, Imagen), generating raster images (.png, .jpg), or outputting Python rendering scripts (matplotlib, opencv).
21	- The entire output MUST be a single, standalone, responsive HTML file containing inline SVGs and formatted tables.
22	
23	## Kinematic Analysis Protocol
24	
25	1. **Dimensionality (m):**
26	   - Planar mechanism: `m = 3`. Formula: `DOF = 3 * (N - 1 - J) + sum(f_i) = 3 * (N - 1) - 2 * J_1 - J_2`.
27	   - Spatial mechanism: `m = 6`. Formula: `DOF = 6 * (N - 1 - J) + sum(f_i)`.
28	2. **Link Identification (N):**
29	   - `L_0`: Ground / fixed base (all fixed pivots, slider tracks, frames count as a single rigid body `L_0`).
30	   - `L_1 ... L_k`: Dynamic rigid bodies (sliders, binary/ternary links, moving platforms).
31	   - Total number of links: `N = 1 + k`.
32	3. **Joint Identification & Classification (J):**
33	   - Classify according to ISO 3952: Revolute (R, f=1), Prismatic (P, f=1), Cylindrical (C, f=2), Fork/Slot (f=2), Spherical (S, f=3), Universal (U, f=2).
34	   - Multiple joints rule: If `k` links coincide at a single common pin, count as `(k - 1)` distinct revolute joints.
35	   - Total number of joints: `J`. Total joint DOFs: `sum(f_i)`.
36	4. **Mobility (DOF):** Calculate `m * (N - 1 - J) + sum(f_i)`.
37	
38	## HTML & Typography Standards
39	
40	- NEVER leak raw unparsed LaTeX (`$`, `$$`) into HTML markup.
41	- Subscripts: use semantic HTML tags `L<sub>0</sub>`, `f<sub>i</sub>`, `J<sub>1</sub>`.
42	- Math symbols: use HTML entities `&times;` (multiply), `&sum;` (summation).
43	
44	## Dual-Panel Visualization Architecture
45	
46	Every generated HTML file must implement a responsive CSS Grid with two distinct panels:
47	
48	### Panel 1: Link Identification (Khau)
49	- High-contrast SVG vector diagram highlighting each distinct link with dedicated semantic colors.
50	- HTML Table listing: Link Symbol (`L<sub>i</sub>`), Link Name, Quantity, and Kinematic Role.
51	
52	### Panel 2: Joint Classification (Khop)
53	- Ghost/muted skeleton background (`#475569`), prominently highlighting joint glyphs and degrees of freedom.
54	- HTML Table listing: Joint Group, Joint Symbol (`J<sub>i</sub>`), Joint Type (ISO), and Freedom Degrees (`f<sub>i</sub>`).
55	
56	## Full HTML Template Boilerplate
